            "pageCount": 1,
            "processed": true,
            "summary": "This article reports a case involving a 45-year-old man who experienced an adverse reaction after taking Neptazol 20mg for the first time. About 30 minutes post-administration, he developed symptoms including facial flushing, throat tightness, and difficulty breathing, indicative of a potential allergic reaction. The patient was treated with intramuscular epinephrine in the emergency department and managed to recover fully within several hours. Following the incident, Neptazol was discontinued and not given to the patient again. \n\nThis document is relevant to a patient-safety review due to the description of a significant adverse reaction following the use of a medication. It highlights the importance of monitoring patients for side effects after starting a new drug, especially if they exhibit serious symptoms like breathing difficulties. The case underscores the need for careful consideration of drug allergies and responses in patients. Additionally, it stresses the importance of immediate action in emergencies, contributing valuable insights for improving safety protocols in medication administration."
        }
